            "url": "https://images.qloo.com/i/D7BCE4CD-5135-4608-8A7D-78E08FFD52F3-420x-auto.jpg"
          },
          "vocals": "Billie Eilish's vocals are characterized by a soft, breathy, and intimate delivery, often using whisper-like tones that create an ethereal and haunting atmosphere. Her vocal style is versatile, ranging from delicate and subdued to more powerful and emotive moments, with a mezzo-soprano range.",
          "aliases": [
            "Billie Eilish Pirate Baird O'Connell"
          ],
          "members": [],
          "is_group": false,
          "biography": "Billie Eilish was born in 2001 in Los Angeles, California. She began singing and writing songs at a young age, collaborating with her brother Finneas who produces much of her music. She first gained attention with the release of her debut single 'Ocean Eyes' in 2015, which went viral online. Her debut album 'When We All Fall Asleep, Where Do We Go?' released in 2019, was critically acclaimed and commercially successful, earning her multiple Grammy Awards. Billie is known for her distinctive fashion style and her candidness about mental health and personal struggles, which resonates with a large global audience.",
          "known_for": "Billie Eilish is known for her distinctive whispery vocal style, dark and moody pop music, innovative production, and her candidness about personal and mental health issues.",
          "start_year": 2015,
          "voice_type": [
            "Mezzo-Soprano"
          ],
          "description": "Billie Eilish Pirate Baird O'Connell is an American singer-songwriter who gained fame as a teenager with her distinctive style blending pop, electropop, and alternative sounds. She is known for her whispery vocals, introspective and often dark lyrical themes, and innovative production, often working closely with her brother Finneas O'Connell. Her music incorporates elements of indie pop, electropop, and dark pop, and she has become a defining figure in contemporary pop music with a strong visual and artistic identity.",
